-- title:
--   Positive-child expansion is charged to one binomial layer
-- statement:
--   Let $h,J,k,t$ be natural numbers with $k<J$. Put $r=(J-k-1)2h$, the residual size after the next block, and assume $t\le\lfloor r/2\rfloor$. Let $G=\binom{2h}{h}$ be the number of balanced children and $B=(J+1)(2048h+20)$. The cost $T(h,J,k,t)$ of expanding a reporting prefix and gathering its positive children satisfies
--   $$
--   T(h,J,k,t)+200\le200000B^4\,G\binom rt.
--   $$
--   The additional $200$ is included in the bound. This converts the implemented expansion cost, with its sparse queries and gathering operations, into the single-layer quantity used by the traversal work ledger.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/SharedTraversalCostBounds.lean#L162-L184

